const description = "Manitowoc ice machine stopped producing? LA same-day diagnostic on Indigo NXT touchscreen alerts + Q-Series + R-Series. EPA 608. BHGS #A49573.";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Why is my Manitowoc ice machine not making ice?",
    a: "A Manitowoc ice machine that stopped making ice usually comes down to one of three things: a water-side fault (closed inlet, scaled inlet valve, clogged supply filter), a bin-sensor or harvest-timing failure stopping the cycle, or a refrigerant-side problem (low charge, weak compressor, fouled condenser). Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair work the diagnostic cheapest-first because about 4 in 5 Manitowoc no-production calls in LA, OC, Ventura, and the IE land on water-side or harvest-side issues before refrigerant work is needed — a $295 service call instead of a $1,200 sealed-system repair. $120 commercial diagnostic, applied toward repair."
  },
  {
    q: "What does 'Long Freeze' mean on my Manitowoc Indigo NXT?",
    a: "Long Freeze on an Indigo NXT touchscreen means the freeze cycle exceeded its design time. Three usual causes in order of frequency: refrigerant under-charge or condenser fouling (sealed-system side), water inlet partial restriction reducing fill speed, or ambient temperature exceeding the unit's spec (kitchen heat exceeding 90°F+ during summer Service). The alert points at the category; our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair confirm the component by checking head pressure on the manifold gauges, inspecting the condenser fins, and timing the water fill. Indigo NXT also stores fault history in the touchscreen menu, which tells us whether Long Freeze has been intermittent or recurring."
  },
  {
    q: "What does 'No Harvest' mean on my Manitowoc Indigo NXT?",
    a: "No Harvest on an Indigo NXT means the freeze cycle completed but ice didn't release from the evaporator during the harvest cycle. Three usual causes: the harvest assist mechanism is stuck or worn (most common on year-5+ IY/IB cubers), the hot gas valve (Acu-Thaw) failed to open and warm the evaporator, or the water curtain switch isn't reading the expected open/closed state during the cycle. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair inspect the harvest assembly and curtain switch first because those resolve roughly 6 of every 10 'No Harvest' calls — Acu-Thaw hot gas valve replacement runs $340 to $540 if that turns out to be the failure."
  },
  {
    q: "What does 'Curtain Switch' alert mean on my Manitowoc?",
    a: "Curtain Switch on an Indigo NXT means the water curtain wasn't detected closed or open at the expected time in the freeze/harvest cycle. The curtain is the hinged flap that closes the freeze chamber during ice formation and opens during harvest; the switch reads its position. Causes: the curtain itself is warped or stuck, the switch is misaligned or failed, or there's a wiring fault between switch and control board. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check curtain alignment first because that's free to rule out — switch replacement runs $185 to $285 if the mechanical inspection clears."
  },
  {
    q: "How do I reset my Manitowoc Indigo NXT ice machine?",
    a: "Indigo NXT resets through the touchscreen menu rather than a physical button: navigate to Service → Reset Faults from the home screen. If the underlying fault is still present, the alert returns within minutes (faster on refrigerant-side faults, slower on intermittent water issues), and the touchscreen Fault History menu preserves the record. On older Q-Series legacy machines without touchscreen, reset is a power-cycle at the breaker. Resetting without diagnosing is fine as a temporary workaround while you wait for our visit; don't ignore an alert that keeps returning. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair read the Fault History first because intermittent patterns point to different parts than steady-state alerts."
  },
  {
    q: "What's the difference between Manitowoc Indigo NXT and Q-Series?",
    a: "Indigo NXT is Manitowoc's current generation (since 2018), replacing the Q-Series legacy line on most new installations. Indigo NXT uses a touchscreen interface with named alerts (Long Freeze, No Harvest, Curtain Switch, Bin Full, High Discharge Temp, Low Water) and the Easy-Read display, plus AlphaSan antimicrobial protection and LuminIce II UV growth inhibitor. Q-Series uses numeric codes similar to Hoshizaki style, simpler display, no AlphaSan or LuminIce II. Q-Series machines are still serviceable through the Welbilt parts network for several more years. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair service both — the diagnostic logic is identical, just the display read changes."
  },
  {
    q: "How long does a Manitowoc ice machine repair take?",
    a: "Time-to-restoration depends on the failure category. Cleaning service: 90 minutes to 2 hours, same-day production restored. Water inlet valve: 60 to 90 minutes on-site, same-day. Harvest sensor or curtain switch: 60 to 90 minutes, same-day. Hot gas valve (Acu-Thaw): 90 to 120 minutes, same-day. Condenser fan motor: 60 to 90 minutes, same-day. Refrigerant leak repair: 3 to 5 hours including leak detection plus evacuation plus recharge, usually same-day for accessible joints, next-day if parts need ordering. Easy-Read board: same-day if a unit on the truck matches; otherwise 1 to 3 day part order. Compressor: full day plus, often next-day completion. Common Indigo NXT parts (inlet valves, harvest sensors, curtain switches, fan motors) are stocked on the van for first-visit completion."
  },
  {
    q: "How much does Manitowoc ice machine repair cost?",
    a: "Diagnostic visit $120, waived with repair. Typical repair line items: cleaning service $200 to $340; water inlet valve $260 to $420; hot gas valve (Acu-Thaw) $340 to $540; harvest sensor $200 to $340; curtain switch $185 to $285; LuminIce II UV bulb $140 to $240; bin sensor $180 to $280; condenser fan motor $300 to $520; Easy-Read display board $480 to $820; refrigerant leak repair plus recharge $700 to $1,500; compressor replacement $1,400 to $2,200 (IB/ID mid-size and undercounter) or $1,800 to $2,800 (IY large modular). Most no-production calls resolve in the $260 to $540 range when the diagnostic points to water-side or harvest-assembly work."
  },
  {
    q: "How often should a Manitowoc ice machine be cleaned?",
    a: "Manitowoc and LA County DPH both recommend 2 to 4 cleanings per year on cube machines — closer to 4 (quarterly) in heavy-use restaurants and bars with hard water, closer to 2 (every 6 months) in lighter-use settings with quality filtration. AlphaSan antimicrobial and LuminIce II UV protection slow biological growth but do NOT prevent mineral scale buildup on the vertical evaporator plate. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair use Manitowoc Cleen Ice brand-spec cleaner during service and document each cleaning for LA County DPH inspection records. Standard cleaning runs $200 to $340 per service; quarterly contracts reduce per-visit cost."
  },
  {
    q: "Why does my Manitowoc ice machine keep stopping mid-cycle?",
    a: "Mid-cycle shutdowns on Manitowoc Indigo NXT usually trigger one of two touchscreen alerts: 'High Discharge Temp' (compressor overheating from fouled condenser or restricted airflow — common when kitchen ambient exceeds 90°F during LA summer service) or 'Long Freeze' (cycle timer exceeded design, often refrigerant under-charge). Less commonly, the curtain switch is intermittent and triggers a 'Curtain Switch' alert mid-cycle. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check the condenser fin condition first because that's the most common root cause on chain restaurant installations where the unit is tucked into a tight kitchen alcove — $245 to $385 cleaning, $300 to $520 if a fan motor replacement is also needed."
  },
  {
    q: "Where can I get Manitowoc parts in LA?",
    a: "Manitowoc parts in LA route through the Welbilt parts network (Wisconsin-based distribution): standard 5 to 7 day ship, expedited 1 to 3 day available for service-critical components. Common Indigo NXT parts (water inlet valves for IY-0454A and IB-0420A, harvest sensors, curtain switches, condenser fan motors for -A air-cooled units, LuminIce II UV bulbs) are stocked on our service trucks for first-visit completion on most LA County hospitality calls. Rarer parts (full Easy-Read display boards, IY-1196A compressors, Q-Series legacy replacements) require Welbilt direct order. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair pre-order based on phone-call symptom description to compress restoration time."
  }
];

